From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: A733 minimal — add SD (mmc0) and eMMC (mmc2)

Milestone-2 storage. Adds the SD (SMHC0 @0x04020000, bank PF) and eMMC
(SMHC2 @0x04022000, bank PC) controllers to the minimal A733 boot DT, plus
two fixed always-on regulators for their supplies and the mmc pin groups.

The controllers reuse the in-tree driver via the "allwinner,sun20i-d1-mmc"
fallback compatible — no new driver code. They consume the SMHC module +
bus-gate clocks and the BGR reset added by patch `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-smhc-pll-peri1-clocks`.

Everything is from live silicon (raw sunxi_dump / regmap on the 6 GiB board SD and the 8 GiB board
eMMC), not a vendor driver:
 - pin groups: SD = PF0..PF5 @ mux 2 (PF_CFG0=0x0e222222); eMMC = the PC pins
   at mux 3. Truth is the schematic (v1.10 p.7): the board wires a full 8-bit
   eMMC, net EMMC-D7 -> PC16; the 8 GiB board silicon (PC_CFG2=0x3) confirms PC16 driven.
   PC2/3/4/12 carry no eMMC net (correctly excluded). Card-detect: schematic
   net SDC0-DET -> PF6/PF-EINT6 (p.7/p.13); the 8 GiB board silicon PF_CFG0=0x0e222222 ->
   PF6 mux 0xe = EINT, as wired. cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6>: on our pinctrl (`pinctrl-sunxi-add-A733-sun60iw2-minimal-pio`)
   banks count PA=0 so PF6 = pin 166 = bank 5 (the 6 GiB board pins: "pin 166 (PF6)",
   "pin 134 (PE6)"). <&pio 4 6> would be PE6. The earlier "bank 4" came from
   the 8 GiB board's vendor 6.6 pinctrl, which compacts banks (PB=0) -- a different
   driver than this DT runs on; the driver only translates, the schematic decides.
 - interrupts: mmc0 = GIC_SPI 161 (SMHC0, INTID 193), mmc2 = GIC_SPI 163
   (SMHC2, INTID 195) -- from the interrupt list of the A733 user manual (UM-derived). The earlier
   SPI 129/131 was WRONG (= INTID 161/163 = CSI_ISP0/CSI_ISP2 camera lines,
   derived backwards from a the 8 GiB board /proc hwirq reading): the mmc completion IRQ
   never fired, both controllers hung mid-attach with no enumeration. HW-proven
   2026-07-18: with 161/163 the IRQ counts rise on I/O and SD + eMMC read.
 - regulators: vmmc = 3.3 V (SWOUT2, AXP318 0x12=0x17), eMMC vqmmc = 1.8 V
   (CLDO5, 0x33=0x0d) — both read = spec on both boards. Modelled as fixed
   always-on: boot0/U-Boot bring the rails up before Linux, so no PMIC driver
   is needed for M2. SD stays non-UHS (vqmmc fixed 3.3 V) until the AXP318
   regulator lands (own later milestone); eMMC HS200 works (VCCQ static 1.8 V).

eMMC is wired even though this unit may ship without it — per-board policy is
to support the full SoC/board capability and let population decide; an eMMC
board (the 8 GiB board) exists for the end-to-end HW proof.

HW proof (boot to rootfs shell, card speed not "it booted") is pending — this
is compile/dtc-gated only.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -12,12 +12,13 @@
  * (earlyprintk=sunxi-uart,0x2500000).
  */
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/reset/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
 
 / {
 	model = "Radxa Cubie A7S (A733 minimal M1)";
 	compatible = "radxa,cubie-a7s", "allwinner,sun60i-a733";
 	interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
@@ -477,12 +478,28 @@
 		#clock-cells = <0>;
 		compatible = "fixed-clock";
 		clock-frequency = <26000000>;
 		clock-output-names = "dcxo26M";
 	};
 
+	reg_vcc3v3: regulator-vcc3v3 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vcc3v3";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
+	reg_vcc1v8: regulator-vcc1v8 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "vcc1v8";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+	};
+
 	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		/* Fallback 1 GiB; the bootloader fixes up the real size. */
 		reg = <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x40000000>;
 	};
 
@@ -535,12 +552,27 @@
 
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
 				function = "uart0";
 			};
+
+			mmc0_pins: mmc0-pins {
+				pins = "PF0", "PF1", "PF2",
+				       "PF3", "PF4", "PF5";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
+				function = "mmc0";
+			};
+
+			mmc2_pins: mmc2-pins {
+				pins = "PC0", "PC1", "PC5", "PC6",
+				       "PC8", "PC9", "PC10", "PC11",
+				       "PC13", "PC14", "PC15", "PC16";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "mmc2";
+			};
 		};
 
 		ccu: clock-controller@2002000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-ccu";
 			reg = <0x0 0x02002000 0x0 0x2000>;
 			clocks = <&osc24M>, <&osc32k>, <&iosc>,
@@ -690,8 +722,55 @@
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_UART0>;
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_UART0>;
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&uart0_pb_pins>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
+
+		mmc0: mmc@4020000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-mmc",
+				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-mmc";
+			reg = <0x0 0x04020000 0x0 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SMHC0>, <&ccu CLK_SMHC0>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mmc";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SMHC0>;
+			reset-names = "ahb";
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 161 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc0_pins>;
+			vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+			vqmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+			cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;	/* PF6 = pin 166; card-in reads HIGH on this board */
+			bus-width = <4>;
+			max-frequency = <150000000>;
+			cap-sd-highspeed;
+			cap-mmc-highspeed;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+
+		mmc2: mmc@4022000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-mmc",
+				     "allwinner,sun20i-d1-mmc";
+			reg = <0x0 0x04022000 0x0 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_SMHC2>, <&ccu CLK_SMHC2>;
+			clock-names = "ahb", "mmc";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_SMHC2>;
+			reset-names = "ahb";
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 163 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&mmc2_pins>;
+			vmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc3v3>;
+			vqmmc-supply = <&reg_vcc1v8>;
+			bus-width = <8>;
+			max-frequency = <150000000>;
+			non-removable;
+			cap-mmc-highspeed;
+			mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+			cap-mmc-hw-reset;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "okay";
+		};
 	};
 };
